---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../config/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How this site measures visits: cookieless, aggregate statistics with Umami, and how to opt out.">
  <header>
    <h1>Privacy &amp; analytics</h1>
    <p>Last updated: November 2026</p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="what">
    <h2 id="what">What is measured</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses <a href="https://umami.is" rel="noopener">Umami Cloud</a>, a privacy-focused analytics service, to count
      visits in aggregate: which pages are viewed, how visitors arrive (the referring website’s domain), country and region,
      device type, browser, and operating system. It also records a few interactions — CV downloads, clicks on GitHub,
      LinkedIn, or email links, which project pages are opened — and an estimate of active reading time and scroll depth per page.
    </p>
    <p>The purpose is to understand which content is useful so the portfolio can be improved. It is not used to identify anyone.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="not">
    <h2 id="not">What is not collected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No cookies are set by the analytics, and no advertising or cross-site tracking is used.</li>
      <li>No names, email addresses, account IDs, or form inputs are collected. This site has no forms or logins.</li>
      <li>URL query strings and fragments are removed before sending, and the referrer is reduced to its domain.</li>
      <li>IP addresses are not stored by this site. Umami processes the request to derive approximate location and an anonymous, periodically rotating visit identifier; see Umami’s documentation for details.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Because no identity is collected, the statistics cannot tell who visited — for example, whether a visitor was from a particular university.</p>
  </section>
